---
description: TypeScript conventions for the library source
globs: src/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

- Strict TypeScript: `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` and `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` are on. Do not widen types to silence errors.
- No `any` in public types. Use `unknown` and narrow.
- Every thrown error from the public API is an `LocalLLMError` with a non-empty `hint`.
- Validate options with the zod schemas in `src/core/schemas.ts`, not ad-hoc checks.
- Keep the hot path (`runRequest`, scheduler, token counting) free of avoidable allocations and awaits.
- Use `biome-ignore` only with a reason on the same line or in a file header, and say why.
